    "bookQuote": "The hand of the Muscular, like all the rest of his body, is built in a series of squares. It runs out from the wrist and down in a straighter line and tends to right angles. (See Chart 6)... Every hand artist will be found to have spatulate-fingered hands\u2014in short, muscular hands.",
    "hciImplication": "Maximum silhouette mass and robust optical presence. The spatulate paddle tips provide wide contact zones for tactile interfaces and high-contrast broadside legibility in emergency sign telemetry.",
